  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Wednesday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: A ridge of high pressure will extend\nwestward across Southern Nevada this afternoon through Friday.\nHigh temperatures in Northern and Central Nevada both this\nafternoon and Friday afternoon will be twelve to fourteen degrees\nabove normal for this time of year. A Western Canada cyclone \naloft will drop southward into the Pacific Northwest Saturday. As \na result, the surface pressure gradient will increase across \nCentral Nevada. A Wind Advisory may be required for parts of \nCentral Nevada due to south to southwest wind gusts near 50 mph. \n\nThe aforementioned upper-level area of low pressure will drop\nsouthward into Northern California Sunday. This storm system will\ndraw atmospheric moisture associated with Tropical Storm Rachel\nnorthward into Eastern Nevada, resulting in the likelihood of rain\nSunday and Sunday night. Rainfall could be heavy at times. A Flood\nWatch may be required. The majority of this rain will fall Sunday\nafternoon and Sunday evening. Here are probabilities of three \nquarters of an inch or more of rain for select locations in \nNorthern and Central Nevada from 5 AM PDT Sunday, October 11th, \n2026 until 5 AM PDT Monday, October 12th, 2026: \n\nEly - 70%\nElko - 60%\nSpring Creek - 55%\nWest Wendover - 55%\nWells - 55%\nCarlin - 50%\nEureka - 50%\nBattle Mountain - 25%\nTonopah - 25%\nWinnemucca - 15% \n\nA cooling trend is expected Saturday through Monday. By Monday\nafternoon, high temperatures across Northern and Central Nevada\nwill be six to eight degrees below normal for this time of year.\nSub-freezing minimum temperatures are anticipated in the valleys \nof Northern and Central Nevada Sunday night through at least \nTuesday night. Maximum temperatures in Northern and Central Nevada\nwill remain below seasonal values Tuesday and Wednesday. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High forecast confidence in\nunseasonably warm temperatures both this afternoon and Friday \nafternoon. High forecast confidence regarding strong wind gusts \nin Central Nevada Saturday and Sunday. High forecast confidence\nregarding significant rainfall in Eastern Nevada Sunday and Sunday\nnight. High forecast confidence in a cooling trend Saturday\nthrough Monday.",
